## Setup & Initialize Database

This project uses Docker and PostgreSQL. To start the application and initialize the database with demo tables and data, run the following commands from the project root:

```bash
# Stop and remove any running containers
docker-compose down

# Remove the Postgres volume so init scripts run fresh
docker volume rm assisment-_pg_data

# Start containers (Postgres will initialize the database)
docker-compose up -d

# Wait a few seconds for Postgres to start
sleep 10

# Run SQL scripts manually to create tables and insert demo data
docker exec -i postgres_db psql -U postgres -d energy_db < db-init/create_tables.sql
docker exec -i postgres_db psql -U postgres -d energy_db < db-init/insert_sample_data.sql

# Verify tables and demo data
docker exec -it postgres_db psql -U postgres -d energy_db -c "\dt"
docker exec -it postgres_db psql -U postgres -d energy_db -c "SELECT * FROM meter_telemetry_history LIMIT 5;"
docker exec -it postgres_db psql -U postgres -d energy_db -c "SELECT * FROM meter_live_status LIMIT 5;"
docker exec -it postgres_db psql -U postgres -d energy_db -c "SELECT * FROM vehicle_telemetry_history LIMIT 5;"
docker exec -it postgres_db psql -U postgres -d energy_db -c "SELECT * FROM vehicle_live_status LIMIT 5;"
